[00:01.50]The chart above clearly reveals the degree of urbani-zation in China 
[00:06.00]during the past 40 years.
[00:09.96]From 1980 to 2010,
[00:12.06]it jumped markedly from 19.39% to 49.95%,
[00:19.81]a rise of approximately 30%.
[00:22.38]The percentage increased steadily from 49.95% to 63.89% 
[00:29.80]between 2010 and 2020,
[00:33.56]a rise of nearly 14%.
[00:36.38]It goes without saying that remarkable achievements have been made 
[00:41.38]in China’s urbanization since the reform and opening- up in the past few decades.
[00:47.77]First and foremost,
[00:49.59]the fundamental contributor for such a sharp increase 
[00:51.59]in urban population results from China’s economic prosperity.
